Keeps a custom vector tile's callbacks after the source reports an error for
it, so invalidating the failed tile fetches it again. Before, setTileError
dropped them, so invalidateTile found nothing, and the tile stayed failed until
it left the view and came back
(https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native-ffi/issues/782).
Upstream: not proposed

diff --git a/src/mln/style/custom_vector_tile_loader.cpp b/src/mln/style/custom_vector_tile_loader.cpp
index b2b4fea..db0a5b2 100644
--- a/src/mln/style/custom_vector_tile_loader.cpp
+++ b/src/mln/style/custom_vector_tile_loader.cpp
@@ -81,7 +81,7 @@ void CustomVectorTileLoader::setTileError(const CanonicalTileID& tileID, std::ex
         auto actor = std::get<2>(tuple);
         actor.invoke(&CustomVectorTile::setTileError, error);
     }
-    tileCallbackMap.erase(iter);
+    // Keep the callbacks, so invalidating the failed tile fetches it again.
     dataCache.erase(tileID);
 }
 
